{"amendments":[{"body":"Legacy timer migration now runs on brand-new states, not just old saves. `StageCohort` still defaults `molt_timer_days` to `0.0` and `AnimalState::default()` still seeds `inter_molt_timer_days` to `14.0` (`crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:105-114`, `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:594-617`). On the first daily tick, the migration branch in `molt_cycle` copies that legacy timer into every stage timer whenever they are all zero (`crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:409-419`). That means a fresh juvenile cohort starts effectively 14 days into a 14-day cycle and can molt immediately, while adults start halfway through their 28-day cycle. The new per-stage cadence therefore does not actually start cleanly for fresh simulations.","rationale":"This changes first-day behavior for every new tank with shrimp and makes the new stage-specific timers behave like migrated legacy state instead of true fresh timers."},{"body":"The per-stage molt loop undercounts failure pressure whenever multiple stages resolve on the same day. Default intervals are 14/21/28 days (`crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:433-438`), so overlaps are guaranteed at days 42 and 84, but the accumulator logic only tracks `any_failed`/`any_succeeded` booleans (`crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:440-442`, `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:467-472`, `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:495-506`). Two or three failed stages still add only one `+0.3`, and a mixed day (one failure plus one success) actually lowers `failed_molt_accum` because both branches run. That makes mortality pressure weakest exactly on the days when more of the population is molting.","rationale":"This is a correctness bug introduced by the new per-stage scheduling: the aggregate failure state no longer scales with the number of failed stage molts and can even move in the wrong direction."},{"body":"The new shrimp preset knobs added in `crates/tank_data/data/shrimp/neocaridina_davidi.toml:23-27` are currently dead configuration. `ShrimpPreset` does not declare `ca_min_mg_per_l`, `mg_min_mg_per_l`, `juvenile_molt_interval_days`, `sub_adult_molt_interval_days`, or `molt_success_threshold` (`crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:430-472`), its metadata helpers do not recognize those names (`crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs:658-733`), and `shrimp_preset_to_params` never copies them into `ShrimpRuntimeParams` (`crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:746-799`). Because TOML deserialization here ignores unknown keys, the file still loads but silently drops all five values.","rationale":"The data file now advertises species-tunable molt parameters that the runtime cannot actually read, which is a silent configuration bug and a trap for future tuning."}],"summary":"Reviewed the diff plus the shrimp runtime/preset plumbing end-to-end. Found three substantive issues: fresh states incorrectly trigger the legacy timer migration path, same-day multi-stage molts undercount or even reverse `failed_molt_accum`, and the new TOML preset fields are silently ignored because the preset/schema mapping was not updated. Targeted tests passed for existing `shrimp_population`, and `cargo test -p tank_core --test molt_mineral_budget` exposed failures consistent with the timer-cadence problems."}